      "problem": "What is the value of $f(s)=⟨{s}^{2},\\,3s-2,\\,-s⟩$ at $s=1?$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate, we substitute $s=1$ into the function, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =⟨{1}^{2},\\,3\\cdot 1-2,\\,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the value of $f(s)$ at $s=1$ is the vector $⟨1,1,-1⟩.$",
